{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1126516-demon-the-fallen-lore-of-the-fundament-in-combat","id":1126516,"title":"[Demon: the Fallen] Lore of the Fundament in Combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T17:40:58-07:00","id":1126516,"title":"[Demon: the Fallen] Lore of the Fundament in Combat?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have some questions regarding level 3 and level 4 of Lore of the Fundament:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) With level 3, it reads: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Roll Dexterity + Athletics. The demon can throw an object up to 30 yards per success rolled, regardless of her Strength. Snatching a projectile out of the air requires rolling a number of successes equal to or greater than the projectile's damage dice. For example, a thrown knife inflicts Strength + 1 damage. If the person throwing the knife has Strength 3, you must roll four or more successes for your character to catch the knife. Your demon has to be able to see the projectile to affect it. Rocks, knives, even arrows are possible candidates, but bullets aren't. If your demon throws a projectile at a target, each extra success achieved becomes an automatic level of damage. The effects of this evocation last for a single turn.<br /> <br /> Would throwing an object do any special amount of damage? If so, how would you do that mechanically?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2) With level 4, it reads: &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Spend one Faith point and roll Dexterity + Athletics. Each success allows your demon to walk up to 10 yards per success per turn, 20 yards per success or run 40 yards per success per turn. If used in combat, treat these successes as automatic levels of damage for hand-to-hand, melee or ranged attacks using thrown weapons. These damage levels can be split among multiple targets if desired. The effects of this evocation last for a single turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Would the Dexterity and Athletics roll be the attack roll? Or would you have to roll this to activate, and then make the attack roll? If using the Dex and Athletics as the attack roll, would you still get to make a damage roll <i>on top of</i> the automatic successes generated from this effect?</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T06:52:44-07:00","id":1127601,"title":"","content":"Ha. We had the same Question(2) in the last session.<br /> We agreed that we handle the evocation roll as the attack roll just for the simplicity.<br /> Nothing is more annoying than to make a roll to see if you're allowed to make a roll.<br /> <br /> I do not understand your first question. It already says &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If your demon throws a projectile at a target, each extra success achieved becomes an automatic level of damage.</span></span></span>&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:02:45-07:00","id":1127608,"title":"","content":"I agree wholeheartedly on the successive dice rolling issue. Your solution was in line with my instincts on the topic as well. With regard to your question - I am wondering if a damage roll is then used on top of the automatic successes. Say 'm stabbing someone using this power. I roll Dex+Athletics, I get 5 successes. I apparently do 4 automatic levels of damage, but would I still roll my strength+2 for the sword I'm wielding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T07:22:21-07:00","id":1127618,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> Like the last time it isn't an absolut answer. It's just like I would handle it.<br /> It's an (with impossible speed) improved attack with a weapon. It should have a attack roll, damage roll and - if so - soak roll.<br /> <br /> The compromise of the effect ruleswise would be that you're making a specialised attack roll (ATH instead of MEL or BRA) and the unsoakable dmg on top.<br /> That's it. I'm aware that little of this is written in the text but it would be my compromise to weave it in the attack sequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T08:10:34-07:00","id":1127646,"title":"","content":"excellent feedback - thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T00:13:00-07:00","id":1127953,"title":"","content":"Hello! did someone called Daddy?. <br /> <br /> Basically lastlostboy nailed it. You has earn icecream, you want icecream, you need icecream, you are worthless without icecreem, you must have it.<br /> <br /> So Yeah, If we marry Physics, the object's velocity would increase due to the lack of any force slowing down, keeping a constant until it clashed against something. you would have to activate the power (Faith), do the roll (to see if you hit or miss). personally i make the very own first roll the same damage roll as well, counting every sucess as a lethal damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}